{
  "title": "Lists — Ordered Containers",
  "subtitle": "Storing Groups of Items Sequentially",
  "topic": "7.1 • LISTS — ORDERED CONTAINERS",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      7.1 • Ordered Collections\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      Python <hlt>Lists</hlt>\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 640px;\">\n      Instead of creating 100 individual variables (e.g. <code>user1</code>, <code>user2</code>), a <strong>List</strong> holds an entire ordered sequence in a single variable!\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #fde047; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      1. Real-World Analogy: Train Compartments\n    </span>\n    <h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      Numbered Seats Starting at Zero\n    </h2>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 12px 0; line-height: 1.5;\">\n      Imagine a train where coaches are numbered <code>[0, 1, 2, 3]</code>. In Python, list indices ALWAYS start at <strong>0</strong>:\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 14px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      tasks = [<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Wake up\"</span>, <span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Code Python\"</span>, <span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Sleep\"</span>]<br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(tasks[<span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">0</span>])   <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Outputs: Wake up (First item)</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(tasks[<span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">2</span>])   <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Outputs: Sleep (Third item)</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(tasks[-<span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">1</span>])  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Negative index: counts from the back -> Sleep</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>"
}